 # PdfCraft roadmap
 
+- 2026-10-15: M8 — partial gray/RGB JPEG redaction preserves uncovered decoded samples and drops JPEG application data, using lossless Flate output; includes save/reopen regression coverage.
+
 **Stage: alpha** · next: beta, ~25% (ready for real work 50% → 75%) and ~400–700 h away
 
 > **Last reviewed:** 2026-10-13 · **Last updated:** 2026-10-14 · **Change:** minor (M14: the Italian catalog has every entry the other catalogs had and the code looks up; estimates unchanged) · **Target:** Adobe Acrobat Pro (Acrobat DC, continuous track 26.002.21931, macOS)
@@ -165,9 +167,8 @@ Ranked; detail and the full milestone table in [docs/roadmap.md](docs/roadmap.md
 - **2026-10-15 (M14, gap 24):** `misc.localization` and `misc.installers` move from planned to partial. Localization: 22 catalogs ship, but Chinese shows tofu in releases, Telugu has no release font and Arabic is not mirrored. Installers: macOS and Windows releases are signed, Linux packages are not. The Acrobat menu diff itself remains open. Estimates unchanged.
 - **2026-10-13 (G14, Vietnamese localization):** Added Vietnamese (`vi`, Tiếng Việt) as an interface and date language with a 2,591-entry catalog (`plural_none`) covering 100% of the current localizable key union (plus `theme`/`Appearance`). Locale tags `vi` / `vi-VN` / `vi_VN.UTF-8` resolve; calendar months use numeric `Tháng 1`…`12` / `tháng 1`…`12`. Native-speaker community review recorded. The twelve-language localization mean moves from ≈59% to ≈68%; weighted readiness ≈49% → ≈50%. Status stays `partial`: engine/OS details, document contents, filenames, CLI/MCP and external help stay outside the catalog by design.
 
-<<<<<<< HEAD
 - **2026-10-14 (M10, Office to PDF):** Word, PowerPoint and Excel files open as new PDFs, converted natively in `pdfcraft-create` (no office suite or sidecar process, web build included): Word sections, styles, lists, tables, images, headers and footers with page fields; PowerPoint slides with master and layout inheritance, theme colours, shapes, pictures and tables; Excel sheets with number formats, fills, borders and merges. Text uses the standard-14 faces, and what can't be drawn (non-Western characters, charts, vector images) is counted in a report. Reachable from File ▸ Open (converted off the UI thread), Create from multiple files, Combine, batch and `doc_create`. Estimates unchanged.
-=======
+
 - **2026-10-12 (M6, XML field names):** AcroForm XML data export constrains generated element names to XML 1.0 NCNames, so Latin-1 names such as `Area²` and `Aµ` produce readable data files. Original PDF field names travel through the existing `xfdf:original` attribute; previously valid tags, including Greek and CJK, keep their spelling. Saved-PDF regressions cover invalid prefixes, combining letters and normalized-name collisions. Estimates unchanged.
 - **2026-10-12 (M6, CSV carriage returns):** Form-data CSV export quotes carriage returns in field names and values, so a trailing carriage return cannot turn into a record separator and disappear on reimport. Saved-PDF round-trip regressions cover CR, LF, CRLF, commas and quotes; estimates unchanged.
 - **2026-10-13 (community, M14, #1553 review):** Relative Fontconfig includes resolve beside each including config, including nested configuration selected through `FONTCONFIG_PATH`. Directory includes accept only digit-prefixed `*.conf` in lexical order. Isolated regressions reproduce both review findings; configuration size/count/depth limits, cycles, symlinked config and valid reset ordering are covered. Estimates unchanged.
@@ -204,7 +205,6 @@ Ranked; detail and the full milestone table in [docs/roadmap.md](docs/roadmap.md
 - **2026-10-14 (M3, control-click candidate):** Coordinate clicks retain hover warmup and pair press/release in one input pass so slow frames do not turn a click into a hold. Text multi-click selection accepts the actual press event when egui has already cleared its origin. Regression cases cover slow-frame button activation, disabled controls and coalesced text selection; estimates unchanged.
 - **2026-10-14 (community, M7, #128 Hebrew in Add text):** Add text and `page_add_text` draw Hebrew with the craft-fonts Hebr face (Noto Sans Hebrew), through the same shaped path as Arabic and Thai: right-to-left display order with numbers and Latin in place, points and cantillation kept on their letter as one Type 3 glyph, ToUnicode and per-line ActualText so extraction, search and the editor get typing order. Builds without the face refuse Hebrew rather than write `?`. Regular style only. Estimates unchanged.
 - **2026-10-14 (M9, #1787):** Changes after signing are judged by the role an object held when signed for a page's resources too: a rewritten font, XObject, graphics state or resources dictionary is page content however its new version is labelled, so a `/FT` or `/Subtype /Widget` added by the attacker no longer reads as a permitted form fill. A category dictionary that only gained a name is judged as before.
->>>>>>> upstream/main
 - **2026-10-13 (M3, native-opening candidate):** Chosen tools survive preparation, conversion and password retries; startup intake waits for pending preparation. Regression tests cover completion, cancellation and document identity. Estimates unchanged.
 - **2026-10-13 (community, M3, #531 touchpad momentum):** On Wayland a two-finger swipe keeps gliding after the fingers lift and slows to a stop, measured from the gesture's last 0.1 s and decaying with a 0.35 s time constant through the #759 1:1 path. Any wheel input, click, key, zoom or edge ends it (fingers resting on the touchpad don't yet: the vendored winit binds no Wayland hold gestures); single-page paging, macOS (which sends its own momentum), the web, and Animation effects Off never glide. Unit tests for the physics and two headless view tests. Estimates unchanged.
 - **2026-10-13 (M3, native-open admission):** Later prepared replies stay queued while a modal or native picker owns the foreground. Picker completion, cancellation and abandonment wake retained opens. Regressions cover recipient ownership, exactly-once admission, source/history preservation and one-shot repaint requests. Estimates unchanged.
